## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of space-time trade-offs in streaming analysis. Introduces hashing-based approximation and how it affects accuracy, latency, and memory.

## Key Concepts
- Hash bucketing for compact counts
- Amortized batch updates
- Probability of collision vs. accuracy
- Space-time trade-offs vs. exact counting

## Code Example
```javascript
class BucketCounter {
  constructor(D) {
    this.D = D;
    this.buckets = new Array(D).fill(0);
    this.max = 0;
  }
  updateBatch(batch, hashFn) {
    for (const c of batch) {
      const b = hashFn(c) % this.D;
      this.buckets[b] += 1;
      if (this.buckets[b] > this.max) this.max = this.buckets[b];
    }
  }
  query(t) { return this.max >= t; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you bound false positives and choose D for a target ε? 
- What changes if batches vary in size or if t scales over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world streaming analytics: maintaining a dynamic feature (distinct count) under batched updates with tight per-batch guarantees. It probes data structures (circular buffers, counters), amortized reasoning, and practical optimizations under constrained space. 

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window maintenance
- Distinct counting with frequency map
- Amortized analysis under batched updates
- Space-conscious data structures and optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation skeleton demonstrating the core idea
class WindowDistinct {
  constructor(W) {
    this.W = W;
    this.buf = new Array(W);
    this.freq = new Map();
    this.head = 0; // points to oldest element
    this.size = 0;
    this.distinct = 0;
  }
  init(arr) {
    for (let i = 0; i < this.W; i++) this.push(arr[i]);
  }
  push(x) {
    if (this.size < this.W) this.size++;
    else {
      this.pop();
    }
    this.buf[this.head] = x;
    this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.W;
    const c = (this.freq.get(x) || 0) + 1;
    this.freq.set(x, c);
    if (c === 1) this.distinct++;
  }
  pop() {
    const idx = (this.head) % this.W;
    const y = this.buf[idx];
    const c = this.freq.get(y) - 1;
    if (c === 0) this.freq.delete(y);
    else this.freq.set(y, c);
    if (c === 0) this.distinct--;
  }
  batchUpdate(batch) {
    for (const x of batch) this.push(x);
  }
  query() {
    return this.distinct;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design batched updates for a non-trivial dynamic property with practical performance guarantees.

## Key Concepts
- sqrt decomposition; block-level DP profiles; mergeable LIS state; amortized update costs.

## Code Example
