## Why This Is Asked
Streaming frequency sketches are common in prod telemetry. This question probes knowledge of CMS, accuracy guarantees, batch processing, and amortized space-time trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Count-Min Sketch (CMS)
- ε, δ error bounds
- Update/query complexity for batches
- Space complexity O(wd)
- Trade-offs vs exact counting

## Code Example
```javascript
// CMS skeleton
const w = Math.ceil(Math.E / eps);
const d = Math.ceil(Math.log(1/delta));
const table = Array.from({length: d}, () => Array(w).fill(0));

function update(x) { for (let i = 0; i < d; i++) table[i][hash_i(i, x) % w]++; }

function query(x) { let m = Infinity; for (let i = 0; i < d; i++) m = Math.min(m, table[i][hash_i(i, x) % w]); return m; }
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would deletions or non-monotone streams affect CMS choices?
- How would you monitor actual error in production without degrading performance?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests dynamic triangle counting with tight amortized analysis, batching, and memory trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic graphs, incremental triangles
- Degree-based edge orientation, forward neighbor sets
- Amortized analysis, batch processing, space efficiency

## Code Example
```javascript
// high-level sketch
const Nplus = Array.from({length: n}, ()=> new Set());
const deg = new Int32Array(n);
let triangles = 0;
function addEdge(u,v){
  // decide orientation
  if (deg[u] > deg[v] || (deg[u]===deg[v] && u>v)) [u,v] = [v,u];
  // count new triangles
  let t = 0;
  for (let w of Nplus[u]) if (Nplus[v].has(w)) t++;
  triangles += t;
  Nplus[u].add(v);
  deg[u]++; deg[v]++;
  // potentially rebalance orientation lazily
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How does the method adapt if deletions are allowed?
- What are practical bottlenecks on real graphs (power-law networks)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical thinking on append-heavy data structures, cache-aware trade-offs, and I/O modeling under realistic constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Two-tier indexing
- Amortized cost analysis
- Cache & I/O modeling
- Rebuild strategies and hot/cold separation

## Code Example
```javascript
class TieredIndex {
  constructor(B) { this.B=B; this.t1=new Map(); this.t2=new Map(); }
  append(blockId, offset) { this.t1.set(blockId, offset); /* trigger rebuild when needed */ }
  lookup(blockId) { if (this.t1.has(blockId)) return this.t1.get(blockId); return this.t2.get(blockId); }
  rebuild() { for (let [k,v] of this.t1) this.t2.set(k,v); this.t1.clear(); }
}
```

